</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="af4409bc-e9a9-4c53-b37a-0821f68aa324">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 6</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>NVDA compatibility: 2026.1 and beyond</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="def93aa0-29fa-4ddd-a2c9-9e0dadcf21af">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 7</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Installation: through the NVDA Add-on Store ([stable version][1])</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="959c7a78-f3a5-4f50-b0b1-4b7627bd6b3a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 9</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Welcome to NVDA Quick Dictionary addon, which will allow you to quickly get a dictionary article with the translation of a word or phrase into your chosen language by pressing a key combination. There are few basic keyboard shortcuts and they are all intuitive and convenient so you will remember them quickly.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="05f8166d-7c5b-4a8c-a387-6f0744c9cad5">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 11</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Dictionary articles contain detailed information about a word, such as part of speech, gender, plural or singular, translation options, list of meanings, synonyms and detailed examples. Such information will be useful for people who are learning foreign languages, or seek to use in communication all the richness and diversity of their own language.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="204a0c93-06cb-4ce6-8530-f77fee9a4f8e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 13</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>The add-on supports several online dictionary services. You can select the desired remote dictionary in the appropriate dialog box or by using keyboard shortcuts. Each available service has its own settings panel.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="ad7ed715-6c34-4100-8dc7-03a51af0c788">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 15</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>There are also advanced opportunities for working with profiles of the voice synthesizers. You can associate a voice synthesizer profile with a specific language, after that translations into this language will be automatically voiced by the selected synthesizer.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="54cb51e4-7adf-4873-8419-73b755b7fb6f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 17</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Below are all the features of the add-on and keyboard shortcuts to control them. By default all functions are called using two-layer commands. But for any of these methods you can always assign convenient for you keyboard shortcuts. You can do it in the NVDA "Preferences" -&gt; "Input gestures..." dialog.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="a488ce80-9cb2-47ea-b51a-2449569f513e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 19</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Receiving a dictionary article</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="63ef6fa7-c12d-49d6-9764-d22c37c5a695">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 20</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>In order to get an article from the dictionary, you must first select the word you are interested in or copy it to the clipboard. Then just press NVDA+Y twice.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="d72e8861-3670-4718-868d-a6630ea84b18">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 22</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>There is also another way to get a dictionary entry: pressing NVDA+Y once switches the keyboard to add-on control mode, then just use the D key.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="9827e6fc-3dc5-444e-9cba-cea63910ae6c">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 24</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Add-on control mode</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="d1cdae5f-f94a-4e92-a21a-161dcd9c7cce">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 25</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>To access all the features of the add-on, you need to switch to add-on control mode, you can do this by pressing NVDA+Y once. You will hear a short low beep and will be able to use the other commands described below. When you press a key that is not used in the add-on, you will hear another signal notifying you of an erroneous command and the add-on control mode will be automatically turned off.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="2bc4ead6-2607-4611-8669-a9b4eab478d9">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 27</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Add-on commands list</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="dc9c6c67-f73c-40c2-a804-862964682c7c">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 28</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Basic dictionary commands:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="41ac6302-1652-44ed-8029-078107d7fca4">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 30</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>D - announce a dictionary entry for a selected word or phrase (same as NVDA+Y);</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0f0ad450-f1ad-43bb-8620-16f307460bf9">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 31</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>W - show dictionary entry in a separate browseable window;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="7485ddce-c475-4a91-880a-761cf15fc21d">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 32</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>S - swap languages and get Quick Dictionary translation;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="4af56d68-3372-44f1-87db-ba215069a241">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 33</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>A - announce the current source and target languages;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="4015ac97-f98f-4436-b247-343a28c062d4">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 34</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>C - copy last dictionary entry to the clipboard;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6d38daee-d6a2-4fdc-b11c-19377f01d3f9">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 35</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>E - edit text before sending;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="0e66e391-885a-4420-ae01-c2bb0e120745">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 36</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>U - download from online dictionary and save the current list of available languages;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="36647ecf-d7f2-4209-8e57-113d4b3ee365">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 37</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>function keys - select online dictionary service;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="67843cdb-f299-4023-9397-afd6b5b1a90a">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 38</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Q - statistics on the using the online service;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="68aacfad-ec4b-4c1b-88e8-e62c2fb29a24">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 39</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>F - choose online service.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="c60ab061-c4e7-427a-96da-3950348bbba7">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 41</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Voice synthesizers profiles management:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="80516c83-5e62-48f3-868e-daef6ed5e14f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 43</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>from 1 to 9 - selection of the voice synthesizer profile;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="f6c5d2d6-6b71-45f3-988b-aea76f16a775">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 44</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>G - announce the selected profile of voice synthesizers;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="ca5332da-c8a4-473a-8bbe-e7a6a6f88482">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 45</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>B - back to previous voice synthesizer;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="30fd10e1-89f4-4325-8455-9d50a00e1ca2">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 46</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>R - restore default voice synthesizer;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="3de46254-b573-4d26-adc4-d4ead91eebd6">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 47</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Del - delete the selected voice synthesizer profile;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="9a618329-5b2d-4c73-9668-0eb8946bfe0e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 48</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>V - save configured voice synthesizer profile;</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="8606b53c-cb56-471a-bdbf-3ea791c0a6d0">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 49</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>P - display a list of all customized voice synthesizers profiles.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="fa67130a-0feb-4cd7-8f50-d28dc7b1ee4e">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 51</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Press O to open add-on settings dialog.</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="ab4d8ab7-06a7-4c39-a7a4-17bf6b3b1d12">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 53</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Help on add-on commands</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="fffbd410-4ba8-42f6-9aed-26d08a8e2afc">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 54</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>You can see a list of all the commands used in the add-on as follows:</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="431d6932-4dd2-42f2-b100-428b0752720f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 56</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Via the NVDA menu - by pressing NVDA+N, go to the submenu "Tools", then - "Quick Dictionary" and activate the menu item "Help on add-on commands".</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="6c6366e2-bea4-4922-a23a-8e2fd95b83be">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 57</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: * </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Press the H key in add-on control mode (NVDA+Y).</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="70d35baf-39a9-43c1-841c-5a1fb07bba55">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 59</note>
<note appliesTo="source">prefix: ## </note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>Add-on help</source>
</segment>
</unit>
<unit id="8ea7756a-b7fd-4963-8a32-5b8cddb8bf3f">
<notes>
<note appliesTo="source">line: 60</note>
</notes>
<segment>
<source>To open the add-on help - press NVDA+N, go to the "Tools" submenu, then - "Quick Dictionary" and activate the menu item "Help".</source>
</segment>
</unit>
